-- חוזר הממונה על השכר 2019-1-6 — תוספת מעונות (זכויות הוריות), עדכון התוספת (17.1.2019)
-- The Wage Controller updates the monthly childcare supplement (parental
-- rights) for a child up to age 5, under clause 11 of the framework
-- agreement of 12.1.2011, by the change in the index (0.8%), from
-- 1.1.2019, and prints the new amounts.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `תוספת מעונות (זכויות הוריות), עדכון התוספת`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 The letterhead (Wage and Labour Agreements, the Ministry of Finance's address), the date (17.1.2019), the circular's number, the addressee (the senior deputy to the Accountant-General) and the subject line; no rule.

-- akn:hc_1/p8 The reference line "חוזרנו - הע-2018-1-5": the previous update, whose amounts this one replaces from 1.1.2019; no rule of its own.

@desc A child for whom the childcare supplement is claimed, as far as this circular asks about it.
DECLARE `child for the childcare supplement` HAS
    `up to age 5`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc the child is "עד גיל 5", the age the circular names; who that is, and who may claim, is clause 11 of the framework agreement of 12.1.2011, which this circular does not restate
    `place among the children`      IS A NUMBER  @desc 1 for "ילד אחד / ילד ראשון" (an only or first child), 2 for "ילד שני" (a second child), counted as clause 11 of the framework agreement counts them

§§ `The update`

-- The date the update takes effect, as printed ("החל מיום"). The amounts
-- below run from it until the next update replaces them, which this
-- circular does not date.
@ref akn:hc_1/p9
`the update takes effect` MEANS Date 1 1 2019

-- The index change as printed, with its sign.
@ref akn:hc_1/p9
`the change in the index` MEANS 0.8%

-- "בהתאם לשיעור השינוי במדד": the supplement moves by the index change. The
-- circular names neither the amount before the update nor a rounding; it
-- prints the result, in whole shekels, below, and the printed amounts are
-- what it sets.
@ref akn:hc_1/p9
GIVEN `the amount before the update` IS A NUMBER @desc the supplement's amount in force before this update, set by the previous year's circular; not printed here
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount moved by the index` `the amount before the update` IS
    `the amount before the update` TIMES (1 PLUS `the change in the index`)

§§ `1–2 The amounts`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_1
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly amount for an only or first child` IS 315

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly amount for a second child` IS 213

-- The circular prints amounts for an only or first child and for a second
-- child, and nothing for any other: whether a third child is paid for is
-- the framework agreement's question, not this circular's, so this circular
-- gives NOTHING there rather than a zero it does not print.
@export default The monthly childcare supplement (in shekels) this update sets for a child, from the date it takes effect
@ref akn:hc_1/p9
GIVEN c       IS A `child for the childcare supplement` @desc the child
      `month` IS A DATE                                @desc a day in the month the supplement is for
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` c `month` IS
    BRANCH IF `month` LESS THAN `the update takes effect` THEN NOTHING
           IF (NOT c's `up to age 5`)                    THEN NOTHING
           IF c's `place among the children` EQUALS 1   THEN JUST `the monthly amount for an only or first child`
           IF c's `place among the children` EQUALS 2   THEN JUST `the monthly amount for a second child`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Payment`

DECLARE `childcare supplement action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the childcare supplement` HAS `childcare amount paid` IS A NUMBER

-- The update is for the employers that pay the supplement: from the date it
-- takes effect they pay it at the updated amount. The circular sets a
-- monthly amount ("לחודש") and no payment date; time here is counted in
-- months from the start of the month the supplement is for, and the
-- supplement is read as due within that month.
@ref akn:hc_1/p9 akn:hc_1__para_1 akn:hc_1__para_2
GIVEN c       IS A `child for the childcare supplement`
      `month` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `childcare supplement action`
DECIDE `the employer pays the updated supplement` c `month` IS
    CONSIDER `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` c `month`
    WHEN JUST due THEN
        PARTY `the employer`
        MUST  `pay the childcare supplement` paid
              PROVIDED paid AT LEAST due
        WITHIN 1
        LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "the childcare supplement was not paid at the updated amount for the month"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off (Kobi Bar-Natan, Wage Controller), the copy to the Civil Service Commissioner, the circular's serial (2019-23) and the department's address; no rule.

§§ `The printed amounts against the printed index change`

-- The amounts in force before this update, as circular 2018-1-5 (corpus circulars-sachar/2018-01_sachar_2018-1-5_maonot, ¶¶1–2), which this circular cites as "חוזרנו".
-- They are used here only to check the printed amounts, never as a rule
-- of this circular.
`the amount in force for an only or first child` MEANS 313
`the amount in force for a second child`         MEANS 211

-- The index change is printed to one decimal of a percent, so the change itself
-- lies within 0.05% of the printed figure.
`the precision of the printed change` MEANS 0.05%

-- A printed amount agrees with the update when some change within the
-- printed precision, applied to the amount in force, rounds to it at the
-- nearest shekel.
GIVEN `before` IS A NUMBER, `after` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the printed amount is the update of` `before` `after` IF
        (`before` TIMES (1 PLUS `the change in the index` MINUS `the precision of the printed change`)) AT MOST (`after` PLUS 0.5)
    AND (`before` TIMES (1 PLUS `the change in the index` PLUS `the precision of the printed change`)) AT LEAST (`after` MINUS 0.5)

#ASSERT `the printed amount is the update of` `the amount in force for an only or first child` `the monthly amount for an only or first child`
#ASSERT `the printed amount is the update of` `the amount in force for a second child` `the monthly amount for a second child`

-- Taken at exactly 0.8%, 313 moves to 315.504, whose nearest shekel is
-- 316; the printed 315 is reached by a change in [0.75%, 0.8%), which the
-- one-decimal figure allows. The printed amount is what the circular sets.
#ASSERT `the amount moved by the index` `the amount in force for an only or first child` GREATER THAN 315.5

§§ `Examples`

`an only child of three` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS TRUE
        `place among the children` IS 1

`a second child of two` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS TRUE
        `place among the children` IS 2

`a third child of one` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS TRUE
        `place among the children` IS 3

`a first child of seven` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS FALSE
        `place among the children` IS 1

#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `an only child of three` (Date 1 1 2019) EQUALS JUST 315
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `a second child of two` (Date 15 3 2019) EQUALS JUST 213
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `an only child of three` (Date 31 12 2018) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `a third child of one` (Date 1 2 2019) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `a first child of seven` (Date 1 2 2019) EQUALS NOTHING
#EVAL   `the amount moved by the index` 100

-- Paid in full within the month, the obligation is fulfilled; paid short,
-- it is still owed.
#TRACE `the employer pays the updated supplement` `an only child of three` (Date 1 2 2019) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the childcare supplement` 315 AT 0
#TRACE `the employer pays the updated supplement` `an only child of three` (Date 1 2 2019) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the childcare supplement` 265 AT 0
